      "writtenOn": "2024-06-21T08:24:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, it is the counter test, which I added in the previous CL. \n\nThe RTC acts as a `counter`, and the counter API is used to [set an alarm](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/main/drivers/timer/cortex_m_systick.c#L251) and wake up CPU.\n\nAdditionally, there is the [COUNTER_RTC_STM32_SUBSECONDS](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/main/drivers/counter/Kconfig.stm32_rtc#L26) config to also used the subsecond register, which increases resolution of the counter (1s tick -\u003e 1/16000s tick IIRC). It is set for the counter tests.",
      "parentUuid": "b3046020_399a2b5a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 10,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 10,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "c8d598822159360c0a70f5af9880c3e6aa4245b1",
